"Read more in our GitHub repository." = "在我們的 GitHub 儲存庫中閱讀更多。";
"You were born without an account" = "您生來就沒有帳號";
"Nobody tracked your conversations. No one drew a map of where you'd been. Privacy was never a feature - it was the way of life." = "沒有人追蹤您的對話。沒有人繪製您去過哪裡的地圖。隱私從來不是一個功能——它是生活方式。";
"Then we moved online, and every platform asked for a piece of you - your name, your number, your friends. We accepted that the price of talking to others is letting someone know who we talk to. Every generation, people and tech, had it this way - telephone, email, messengers, social media. It seemed the only way possible." = "然後我們轉到線上，每個平台都要求您的一部分——您的名字、您的號碼、您的朋友。我們接受了與他人交談的代價是讓某人知道我們在和誰說話。每一代人，無論是技術還是普通人，都是這樣——電話、電子郵件、通訊軟體、社群媒體。似乎是唯一的方式。";
"There is another way. A network with no phone numbers. No usernames. No accounts. No user identities of any kind. A network that connects people and carries encrypted messages without knowing who is connected." = "還有另一種方式。一個沒有電話號碼的網路。沒有使用者名稱。沒有帳號。沒有任何形式的使用者身份。一個連接人們並傳遞加密訊息而不知道誰被連接的網路。";
"Not a better lock on someone else's door. Not a nicer landlord that respects your privacy, but still keeps the record of all visitors. You are not a guest. You are home. No king can enter it - you are sovereign." = "不是別人門上更好的鎖。不是尊重您隱私但仍記錄所有訪客的更好的房東。您不是客人。您在家。沒有國王能進入——您是主權者。";
"Your conversations belong to you, as it had always been before the Internet. The network is not a place you visit. It is a place you create and own. And nobody can take it from you, whether you make it private or public." = "您的對話屬於您，就像在網際網路之前一直那樣。網路不是您造訪的地方。它是您建立和擁有的地方。沒有人能從您那裡奪走它，無論您使它私密還是公開。";
"The oldest human freedom - to speak to another person without being watched - built on infrastructure that cannot betray it." = "最古老的人類自由——在不受監視的情況下與另一個人交談——建立在無法背叛它的基礎設施上。";
"Because we destroyed the power to know who you are. So that your power can never be taken." = "因為我們摧毀了知道您是誰的權力。這樣您的權力就永遠無法被奪走。";
